<svg viewBox="0 0 720 400" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" role="img" aria-label="Three levels of similarity measurement against reference data">
  <!-- reference -->
  <rect x="170" y="16" width="380" height="44" rx="9" fill="var(--accent-soft)" stroke="var(--accent)" stroke-width="1.5" />
  <text x="360" y="36" font-size="12.5" font-weight="600" text-anchor="middle" fill="var(--accent-ink)">Reference response</text>
  <text x="360" y="52" font-size="11.5" text-anchor="middle" fill="var(--ink-soft)">“My cats scare the mice”</text>

  <!-- row 1: exact match -->
  <rect x="40" y="92" width="200" height="84" rx="9" fill="var(--bg-inset)" stroke="var(--line-strong)" />
  <text x="140" y="116" font-size="13" font-weight="600" text-anchor="middle" fill="var(--ink)">Exact match</text>
  <text x="140" y="136" font-size="10.5" text-anchor="middle" fill="var(--ink-soft)">candidate must equal a reference</text>
  <text x="140" y="152" font-size="10.5" text-anchor="middle" fill="var(--ink-soft)">binary · works for short answers:</text>
  <text x="140" y="168" font-size="10.5" text-anchor="middle" fill="var(--ink-soft)">“2 + 3?” → “5”</text>

  <!-- row 2: lexical -->
  <rect x="260" y="92" width="200" height="84" rx="9" fill="var(--bg-inset)" stroke="var(--line-strong)" />
  <text x="360" y="116" font-size="13" font-weight="600" text-anchor="middle" fill="var(--ink)">Lexical similarity</text>
  <text x="360" y="136" font-size="10.5" text-anchor="middle" fill="var(--ink-soft)">do the texts LOOK alike?</text>
  <text x="360" y="152" font-size="10.5" text-anchor="middle" fill="var(--ink-soft)">token overlap · edit distance</text>
  <text x="360" y="168" font-size="10.5" text-anchor="middle" fill="var(--ink-soft)">n-grams · BLEU, ROUGE…</text>

  <!-- row 3: semantic -->
  <rect x="480" y="92" width="200" height="84" rx="9" fill="var(--bg-inset)" stroke="var(--line-strong)" />
  <text x="580" y="116" font-size="13" font-weight="600" text-anchor="middle" fill="var(--ink)">Semantic similarity</text>
  <text x="580" y="136" font-size="10.5" text-anchor="middle" fill="var(--ink-soft)">do the texts MEAN the same?</text>
  <text x="580" y="152" font-size="10.5" text-anchor="middle" fill="var(--ink-soft)">embed both → cosine similarity</text>
  <text x="580" y="168" font-size="10.5" text-anchor="middle" fill="var(--ink-soft)">BERTScore, MoverScore…</text>

  <!-- example comparisons -->
  <g font-size="11">
    <rect x="40" y="208" width="640" height="56" rx="8" fill="var(--bg-raised)" stroke="var(--line)" />
    <text x="58" y="231" fill="var(--ink)">candidate A: “My cats eat the mice”</text>
    <text x="58" y="250" fill="var(--ink-soft)">exact: ✗ no match · lexical: 4/5 words shared → 80% · semantic: high (same scene, different verb)</text>

    <rect x="40" y="276" width="640" height="56" rx="8" fill="var(--bg-raised)" stroke="var(--line)" />
    <text x="58" y="299" fill="var(--ink)">candidate B: “What’s up?” vs reference “How are you?”</text>
    <text x="58" y="318" fill="var(--ink-soft)">exact: ✗ · lexical: ~0% overlap · semantic: high — only embeddings see that these mean the same thing</text>
  </g>

  <text x="360" y="368" font-size="12" font-style="italic" text-anchor="middle" fill="var(--ink-soft)">Pitfalls go the other way too: “Let’s eat, grandma” vs “Let’s eat grandma” — lexically near-identical, semantically… not.</text>
  <text x="360" y="388" font-size="12" font-style="italic" text-anchor="middle" fill="var(--ink-soft)">And all three depend on references being present and correct — a real weakness in practice.</text>
</svg>
